<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai Precision bonds to buy facilities.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Precision bonds to buy facilities.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hyundai Precision and Industries Co would use $70 million in convertible bonds for replacement and new purchases of facilities, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bonds, issued in London on Wednesday, have a coupon rate of 0.25 percent and a maturity date of December 31, 2007.</p>
<p>Joint lead managers of the issue were Bankers Trust and Hyundai Securities.</p>
</text>
